Nav2 Planner & Controller Comparison Results
============================================

Test Configuration:
- Start Position: [-2.71, -2.95, theta]
- Goal Position: [4.20, 2.28, theta]
- Date/Time: 2026-01-28 14:35

Standard Navigation Challenge Results:
--------------------------------------

Test 1: NavFn + DWB (Baseline)
- Navigation Time: 43.64 seconds
- Path Length: 10.53 metres (measured using RViz Measure tool in segments)
- Success: Yes
- Number of Visible Replans: 4
- Path Characteristics:
  * Smoothness (1-5): 4
  * Wall clearance (close/medium/far): Medium
- Observations: Minor corrective behaviour was observed near the goal, 
with the robot briefly steering towards the wall before stabilising.

Test 2: Theta Star + DWB
- Navigation Time: 45.41 seconds
- Path Length: 10.56 metres (measured using RViz Measure tool in segments)
- Success: Yes
- Number of Visible Replans: 6
- Path Characteristics:
  * Smoothness (1-5): 4
  * Wall clearance (close/medium/far): Far
- Observations: The planned path appeared smoother than NavFn, with fewer abrupt direction
 changes, although this resulted in a slightly wider trajectory and increased replanning.

Test 3: Smac 2D + DWB
- Navigation Time: 45.60 seconds
- Path Length: 13.44 metres (measured using RViz Measure tool in segments)
- Success: Yes
- Number of Visible Replans: 5
- Path Characteristics:
  * Smoothness (1-5): 3
  * Wall clearance (close/medium/far): Close
- Observations: The planner produced a longer and more conservative path. While initial
corner avoidance was effective, the robot later executed sharper turns, 
reducing overall smoothness.

Test 4: NavFn + Regulated Pure Pursuit
- Navigation Time: 44.19 seconds
- Path Length: 10.26 metres (measured using RViz Measure tool in segments)
- Success: Yes
- Number of Visible Replans: 4
- Path Characteristics:
  * Smoothness (1-5): 5
  * Wall clearance (close/medium/far): Medium
  * Corner behaviour: Curved around the corner
- Observations: The controller followed the planned path smoothly with continuous 
curvature, reducing abrupt velocity changes and improving 
overall motion stability.

Test 5: DWB + NavFn (Verification)
- Navigation Time: 44.57 seconds
- Path Length: 10.44 metres (measured using RViz Measure tool in segments)
- Success: Yes
- Number of Visible Replans: 2
- Path Characteristics:
  * Smoothness (1-5): 4
  * Wall clearance (close/medium/far): Medium
  * Corner behaviour: Giving space to the corners
- Observations: Results closely matched the baseline test, confirming
consistency in the experimental setup and validating the repeatability 
of the measurements.

Comparative Analysis:
--------------------
Best for speed: NavFn + DWB  
Best for smoothness: NavFn + Regulated Pure Pursuit  
Best for tight spaces: NavFn + DWB  
Most predictable: NavFn + Regulated Pure Pursuit  

Trade-offs observed: NavFn produced shorter and faster paths but showed sharper 
corner behaviour with DWB. Theta Star had smoother and wider paths, 
resulting in increased replanning and slightly longer navigation times. 
Smac 2D prioritised safe paths, leading
to significantly longer distances. Regulated Pure Pursuit improved smoothness 
and predictability when following NavFn paths but less responsive compared to DWB.

