============================================================
Challenge B — Recovery Behaviour
============================================================

Test | Initial Error           | Particle Behaviour                         | Result
-----+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+--------
1    | ~1 m offset             | Spread initially, then tightened            | Success
2    | ~2.5 m + 90–180° offset | Divergence, no stable convergence           | Failed
3    | Kidnapped mid-run       | Full spread, partial convergence observed   | Failed

Key Observation:
Small initial pose errors are recoverable by AMCL, with particle clouds
successfully converging after brief spreading. Large positional and
rotational errors, as well as mid-navigation kidnapping, lead to particle
divergence or unstable localisation, preventing reliable navigation.

Key Finding:
AMCL recovery is effective for minor localisation errors but fails under
large pose discrepancies or sudden relocation, highlighting the importance
of accurate initialisation and distinctive environmental features.

